title: Invoice
+++
% // A page a message is addressed to. Its name is its path without the
% // extension, "/" written as ".", so this is `handlers.invoice` — no
% // front matter declares it and nothing registers it.
% //
% // Delivered, it renders with the message bound as `req`, exactly as it
% // would under $.render(name, data). Whether the caller waited for the
% // answer is not this page's business: rendered inline it returns a
% // tree, delivered from a queue it runs for its effects.
% //
% // `req.msg` is the one thing a delivery adds — the envelope, so a page
% // can dedupe on (name, index) or notice it is being retried.
= Invoice for {{ req.customer }}

Order {{ req.id }} — ${{ req.total }} due.

% // ...and the next step of the workflow. This is NOT a reply: nobody is
% // waiting for it. The chain of pages IS the workflow, and it only goes
% // out once this render has succeeded.
% $.publish("handlers.mailer", { to: req.customer, about: req.id })
